  "segments": [
   {
    "id": "t1",
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 5.2,
    "text": "So at year one, you should have five separate visits for vaccines rather than giving them all in the same day."
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "start": 5.2,
    "end": 8.72,
    "text": "An executive order does not replace scientific evidence."
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "start": 8.72,
    "end": 11.92,
    "text": "The combination MMR vaccine has been shown to be safe."
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "start": 11.92,
    "end": 14.48,
    "text": "There is no evidence that it needs to be separated."
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "start": 14.48,
    "end": 17.2,
    "text": "That just means unnecessary extra visits."
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "start": 17.2,
    "end": 19.44,
    "text": "More days off to take your babies in."
   },
   {
    "id": "t7",
    "start": 19.44,
    "end": 20.64,
    "text": "More co-pays."
   },
   {
    "id": "t8",
    "start": 20.64,
    "end": 21.92,
    "text": "More needle sticks."
   },
   {
    "id": "t9",
    "start": 21.92,
    "end": 24.56,
    "text": "And a higher likelihood of missing doses."
   },
   {
    "id": "t10",
    "start": 24.56,
    "end": 28.48,
    "text": "Also, there has been no evidence that any of the childhood vaccinations cause autism."
   },
   {
    "id": "t11",
    "start": 28.48,
    "end": 30.8,
    "text": "Leave healthcare to the healthcare professionals."
   }
  ]
 },
